@startuml
!include <C4/C4_Container>
title Container - Todo app @ v0.0.1

Person(user, "End user", "A person who manages their personal todo list")

System_Boundary(b, "Todo app") {
  Container(client, "client (Todo SPA)", "React 19 SPA (static HTML/CSS/JS executed in browser)", "Todo UI: loads static assets, runs React in the browser, calls /api/todo via fetch.")
  Container(server, "server (API & static)", "Hono 4 on Bun", "REST /api/todo CRUD + /api/health (DB probe); CORS; persists todos in SQLite; in production also serves the built SPA (client/dist) with SPA fallback.")
}

Rel(user, client, "Uses the SPA", "HTTP (browser)")
Rel(client, server, "CRUD todos", "HTTP JSON /api/todo")

note bottom of b
  shared package provides TypeScript types only (compile-time dependency, not a runtime container).
  Todos are persisted in a SQLite file inside the server container (DATABASE_PATH, default ./data/todo.db), migrated on boot.
  The embedded AI edge keeps Mastra conversation memory in a separate SQLite file (MEMORY_DATABASE_PATH, default ./data/memory.db), created on first agent run.
  The HTTP API and the embedded AI edge share the same todo store; Mastra memory uses its own tables.
  In production the server also serves the built SPA static files (client/dist) with SPA fallback (same-origin).
end note

SHOW_LEGEND()
@enduml
